    "Alphabet (Google)": {revenue:69, total:403, buyer:true, people:0, profit:0, conf:"derived",
      scope:"Hardware purchases only: servers (incl. TPU/GPU systems, storage servers), networking equipment, and Pixel/Nest/wearables device hardware. Excludes data-center land, buildings, power and cooling, offices, and leases. Also includes the chip-design EDA and IP licences shown, for its in-house chips.", period:"CY2025 (fiscal year ended Dec 31, 2025)",
      otherLabel:"Other hardware suppliers (Celestica, Arista, Cisco, ...)",
      outside:[{label:"Advertising, cloud & subscription customers", usd:69}],
      basis:"Total 2025 capex was $91.4B (10-K; quarters of $17.2B, $22.4B, $24.0B and $27.9B). On the Q4 call the CFO said about 60% went to servers and 40% to data centers and networking equipment, which gives servers of about $55B (Q3 was also 60/40, Q2 about two-thirds). Networking is assumed to be about a quarter of the 40% bucket, about 10% of capex or about $9B; the rest is land, buildings and power/cooling. The 10-K says servers plus network equipment are about 60% of gross in-service technical-infrastructure assets, which fits a roughly 70% hardware share of yearly spending, because buildings stay on the books far longer than servers. Device hardware outside capex adds about $5B (about 12M Pixels plus Nest and wearables, parts plus assembly), for about $69B in total, with a range of roughly $60-75B. Measuring on an accrual basis would add about $3B (capex in accrued liabilities and accounts payable rose $4.8B to $15.1B), which roughly offsets the part of capex that is not technical infrastructure. Tracked suppliers account for $39.7B (58%), leaving about $29.3B for other hardware suppliers.",
      sources:[{title:"Alphabet 2025 Form 10-K - cash flow (purchases of P&E $91,447M; accrued capex $15,090M), PP&E note (servers + network ~60% of technical infrastructure), total revenues $402,836M", url:"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1652044/000165204426000018/goog-20251231.htm"}, {title:"Alphabet Q4 2025 earnings call transcript (Feb 4, 2026) - CapEx $27.9B Q4 / $91.4B FY; ~60% servers, 40% data centers and networking equipment", url:"https://s206.q4cdn.com/479360582/files/doc_events/2026/Feb/04/2025_Q4_Earnings_Transcript.pdf"}, {title:"Alphabet Q3 2025 earnings call transcript (Oct 29, 2025) - CapEx $24B; ~60% servers, 40% data center and networking equipment", url:"https://s206.q4cdn.com/479360582/files/doc_events/2025/Oct/29/2025_Q3_Earnings_Transcript.pdf"}, {title:"DatacenterDynamics - Google spends almost $15bn on servers in Q2 2025", url:"https://www.datacenterdynamics.com/en/news/google-spends-almost-15bn-on-servers-in-q2-says-cloud-still-in-tight-supply-and-demand-position/"}, {title:"Celestica 2025 Form 10-K - revenue $12.39B; customers include Google; three 10%+ customers at 32%/14%/12%", url:"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1030894/000103089426000011/cls-20251231.htm"}, {title:"Mobile World Live (citing Nikkei Asia) - Pixel shipments around 12 million units in 2025", url:"https://www.mobileworldlive.com/?p=511358"}]},
